Bugfix: Report errors when closing restored files in the `restore` command

Since restic 0.19.0, errors returned when closing restored files were
silently ignored, so a restore could exit successfully even though some
files were incomplete or corrupt, for example on filesystems that only
report write failures when a file is closed. Restic now reports these
errors and the restore fails instead of exiting successfully.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22179
